],"best_idea":"A saving throw that prorates the effect in a band just below the roll (100 minus 5 per point below the save), with immunity checked before the resist term, so partial resistance is a curve rather than all-or-nothing.","decision":"adapt","decision_why":"The stat-to-modifier table and the prorated save fit the magic and mind systems and can be data-driven; adapt because the donor seeds RNG from frame counts (D1, D2), drops skill-use excess (D3), and has null-cast risks on civilian targets (D6, D7) that must be fixed first.","decision_status":"proposed","acceptance":"A caster with Will 60 facing a mind effect has save 50 + 6 = 56: a roll of 60 gives 100 percent of the effect, 40 gives 20 percent and 30 gives 0 percent; a server test asserts those three values with the RNG injected."}
